    "abstract": "Parts figure for the wing lower cover between ribs 8 and 14 on the four-engine stretched aircraft, showing the stringer kits, the spar cap, the skin panel and the harness clamping across the run-out region.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "This figure identifies the lower cover items in the stringer run-out region between ribs 8 and 14, including the reinforced stringer kit and the harness clamps that move with it.",
      "figure_note": "Sheet 1 shows the left wing lower cover looking up with the tank access panels removed; the right wing is a mirror image. Sheet 2 shows the run-out detail at a single stringer. Item 10 is the reinforced stringer kit with the tapered pad integral and item 10A is the original stepped-taper stringer; the two are not interchangeable, because the fastener pitch of the last three rows differs and the spar cap is drilled to match. Item 10A is listed for identification only and is no longer supplied, so any stringer replacement brings the aircraft to the reinforced standard and the spar cap has to be re-drilled with it. Item 50 clamp positions move 40 mm inboard on reinforced aircraft and both lines are dimensioned on sheet 2."
    },
